                What Is a Tennis Ball Collector <span class="text-t-green">and Why It Matters</span>
              </h2>
              
              <p class="text-t-off-white sm:text-lg text-base font-pluto leading-relaxed">
                Manual ball pickup wastes <span class="text-t-green">20–30% of on-court time</span>. Every few minutes, play stops as players collect scattered balls, disrupting rhythm and reducing valuable practice time.
              </p>
              
              <p class="text-t-off-white sm:text-lg text-base font-pluto leading-relaxed">
                A <span class="text-t-green">tennis ball collector</span> eliminates this downtime entirely. Instead of stopping drills to gather balls, an automated system continuously collects them while you play, maintaining training flow and maximizing court productivity.
              </p>
              
              <p class="text-t-off-white sm:text-lg text-base font-pluto leading-relaxed">
                The Tennibot Rover revolutionizes ball collection with <span class="text-t-green">AI-powered tracking and navigation</span>. Unlike manual collectors that simply assist with a tedious chore, the Rover eliminates the task entirely by autonomously navigating the court to efficiently locate and collect tennis balls automatically.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="h-[50vh] md:h-[60vh] lg:h-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
